      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring 500 ml of water to the boil. Add the lemongrass, galangal, kaffir lime leaves, shallots, and chilli. Simmer for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in the {{coconut-milk}}. Reduce to a low simmer."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add 200 g of sliced mushrooms (chestnut or shiitake work well) and the tofu cubes. Simmer for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season with {{soy-sauce-light}} and lime juice. Taste for balance. The soup should be creamy, mildly sour, and savoury."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ladle into bowls. Top with spring onions and fresh coriander. Serve immediately with jasmine rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Coconut milk has curdled",
              "cause": "Soup boiled too hard after coconut milk was added",
              "fix": "Reduce heat immediately. A gentle simmer only. Whisk briefly to re-emulsify if it splits slightly."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Soup tastes flat without fish sauce",
              "cause": "Soy sauce alone lacks the depth of fish sauce",
              "fix": "Add a small pinch of salt and a few extra drops of lime juice. A tiny amount of miso stirred in at the end also helps."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Tofu has disintegrated",
              "cause": "Simmered too long",
              "fix": "Add tofu in the last 5 minutes and handle gently. Never stir vigorously once it is in."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thai coconut soups like tom kha are deeply fragrant and comforting. This vegan version appears on menus across Thailand's Buddhist temples and vegetarian restaurants. The aromatics do the heavy lifting. Lemongrass, galangal, and kaffir lime leaves create a broth that tastes rich and complex even without meat. Mushrooms add an umami depth that partly compensates for the absence of fish sauce. This is a soup that rewards good coconut milk and freshly squeezed lime juice."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
